WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.601
[dramatic music playing]

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.604
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER): 30
miles north of Petra, I'm

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:07.607
laser scanning the
ancient city of Sela

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:08.608
for the very first time.

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:16.282
I'm looking for clues that the
nomadic Nabateans settled here.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.758
Look at this.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.694
There's pottery just, like,
falling out of the ground.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:31.898
That's the indication
for people living here.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.166
This is somebody's
fingerprint.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.869
Yes, exactly.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.804
My finger fits perfectly.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.272
That's crazy.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.541
You can just feel
somebody's fingerprint

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:44.043
right here, locked in time.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.211
Mhm.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:46.679
Unbelievable.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.415
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER): The
pottery proves people were

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:53.219
here, but it's not clear who.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.755
It could simply be the guards
charged with protecting

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.758
the Nabateans' treasure.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.093
Look at this.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.060
You got a staircase.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.829
Where does it go?

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:03.797
Up.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.598
[instrumental music playing]

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.711
Probably it's a place to pray.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.079
Yes, absolutely.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:20.914
You think so?

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.348
Yeah.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:25.718
You look for a high place
to be closer to the gods.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.426
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
So far, all

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:37.130
I've found is a piece of
pottery and an ancient stairway

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:38.431
to heaven.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:41.468
I guess this is
all sandstone, right?

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.502
Yes, it is.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.904
So over 2,000
years, the landscape

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.673
has sort of melted away.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.511
ALBERT LIN
(VOICEOVER): The desert

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:55.081
winds and winter rains are
eroding the soft sandstone

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.382
into strange shapes.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:05.492
But I can just make out curious
regular markings in the rocks.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:11.931
What are these
little holes up here?

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:15.902
Well, actually, this is the
traditional Nabatean house.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:18.137
So they were living here.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.340
And you can see the
marks of the axe

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:24.344
that they have been
using to carving.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.813
These are chisel
marks, yes, exactly.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.115
Somebody was just sitting
here, chiseling away, creating

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:32.485
a space for their family maybe.

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.020
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
Carving caves

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.990
into dwellings suggested they
spent long stretches of time

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.626
here.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.128
Look at the
beautiful view here.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.330
It's unbelievable.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.164
This is the east.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.499
The sun will come up.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:49.802
It will be sunny in this spot.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.337
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
The cave's position

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:54.007
reveals the reason for the
strange regular markings

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.342
above the entrance.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.045
They're post holes
for their tent poles.

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:03.983
You have this, you know,
shelter in front of your house.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.987
So they've gone from living
in tents to combining tents

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.355
with living in stone then.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.427
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
The evidence

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:17.330
is stacking up that homes
were created at Sela.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:25.405
But it's hot, exposed,
and desert dry,

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:28.107
without a single water
source on the whole outcrop.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.380
No one can survive
without water.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:37.216
So how did the Nabateans?

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:40.320
I'm hoping my Lidar data
can help solve the mystery.

